  "metadata": {
    "title": "Smoothing: estimate unseen mass, then reward new contexts",
    "description": "Good\u2013Turing estimates unseen probability mass as N1/N and discounts rare counts using frequency-of-frequencies. Kneser\u2013Ney uses continuation probability: the number of distinct left contexts a word completes. In the example, coffee has more distinct contexts than the more frequent word Angeles."
  }
